{"id": "85902", "name": "המרת רדיאנים למעלות – π/n (באנגלית)", "defaultgrade": 1, "penalty": 0.1, "options": {"multiplicationsign": "dot", "complexno": "i", "matrixparens": "[", "inversetrig": "cos-1", "logicsymbol": "lang", "sqrtsign": true}, "nhints": 0, "questiontext": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"background:#F4F1F5;border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px\"><p>To how many degrees do \\(\\frac{\\pi}{{CT:0}}\\) radians correspond?</p></div><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:14px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><p>An angle of \\(\\frac{\\pi}{{CT:0}}\\) radians can also be described as being</p><div style=\"background:#FAF9FB;border-radius:8px;padding:10px;direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate\">[[input:ans1]] degrees.</div><div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"direction:ltr;text-align:center;unicode-bidi:isolate;margin-top:6px\">[[validation:ans1]]</div></div></div>", "generalfeedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\" style=\"max-width:980px;font-family:Arial;line-height:1.7\"><div style=\"border:1px solid #D9D1DD;border-radius:12px;padding:14px 16px;margin:12px 0;overflow-x:auto\"><b style=\"color:#4b1f6f\">Radians to degrees</b><br>There are {{CT:1}} radians in a revolution; \\(\\pi\\) radians correspond to \\(180\\) degrees. The number of degrees equivalent to \\(\\frac{\\pi}{{CT:0}}\\) radians is \\(\\frac{\\pi}{{CT:0}}\\) multiplied by \\(\\frac{180}{\\pi}\\), which is<p dir=\"ltr\" style=\"text-align:center\">\\[ {{CT:2}}^{\\circ}. \\]</p></div></div>", "specificfeedback": "<p>[[feedback:Result]]</p>", "prtcorrect": "<span class='correct'>Correct answer, well done.</span>", "prtpartiallycorrect": "<span class='partially'>Your answer is partially correct.</span>", "prtincorrect": "<span class='incorrect'>Incorrect answer.</span>", "inputs": [{"name": "ans1", "type": "algebraic", "boxsize": 20, "insertstars": 0, "forbidfloat": true, "forbidwords": "*", "allowwords": "", "mustverify": true, "showvalidation": 1, "syntaxhint": "", "syntaxattribute": 0, "options": "", "requirelowestterms": true}], "prts": [{"name": "Result", "value": 1, "autosimplify": true, "feedbackstyle": 1, "feedbackvariables": "", "firstnode": 0, "nodes": [{"name": 0, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "degrees", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 1, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "GEO-ANM-TRUE", "feedback": ""}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 1, "answernote": "GEO-AMN-FALSE0", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 1, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "degrees*2", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "GEO-AMN-1-FALSE", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Remember there are {{CT:1}} radians in a revolution, not \\(\\pi\\) radians.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 2, "answernote": "GEO-AMN-FALSE1B", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 2, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "degrees/2", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "GEO-AMN-2-FALSE", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">Remember there are {{CT:1}} radians in a revolution, not {{CT:3}} radians.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 3, "answernote": "GEO-AMN-FALSE2B", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 3, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "recipmult", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": -1, "answernote": "GEO-AMN-3-FALSE", "feedback": "<div dir=\"ltr\">This is \\(\\frac{\\pi}{{CT:0}}\\) degrees in radians.</div>"}, "on_false": {"scoremode": "=", "score": 0, "nextnode": 4, "answernote": "GEO-AMN-FALSE3B", "feedback": ""}}, {"name": 4, "answertest": "AlgEquiv", "sans": "ans1", "tans": "recipmult/2", "testoptions": null, "quiet": false, "on_true": {"scoremode": "=", 